,title,link,text,language,family
0,Yinggarda language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yinggarda_language,"The Yinggarda language (also written Yingkarta and Inggarda) is an Australian Aboriginal language. It is an endangered language, but efforts at language revival are being made.",Yinggarda,Australian
1,Yingkarta - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yingkarta,"Yinggarda was a Kartu language spoken from the coastal area around Carnarvon through the Gascoyne River to the junction and southwards to the Wooramel River. The earliest record of the languages dates from material collected by an anonymous source and forwarded by Edric Gifford to Edward Curr, who published a list of basic words in 1886. [1][2] There were two dialects, a northern and southern ...",Yinggarda,Australian
2,Yinggarda | Smithsonian Folkways Recordings,https://folkways.si.edu/albert-and-rosie/song-by-albert-and-rosie/world/music/track/smithsonian,"Albert and Rosie (Yinggarda), Carnarvon, Western Australia From Songs of Aboriginal Australia and Torres Strait Audio Yinggarda Buy Track0.99 Join our email list for the latest news from Smithsonian Folkways Recordings Click to join mailing list Support our non-profit mission with a monthly donation and enjoy streaming access to the collection via our website Become a Friend of Folkways",Yinggarda,Australian
3,Yinggarda (2) - YouTube,https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=R0ORR4Er6NM,"Provided to YouTube by The Orchard Enterprises Yinggarda (2) · Albert and Rosie (Yinggarda), Carnarvon, Western Australia · Unspecified Songs of Aboriginal Australia and Torres Strait ℗ 1964 ...",Yinggarda,Australian
4,Songs of Aboriginal Australia and Torres Strait - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_neZgQDfLMrlJEQg_OmS1o9ifTGERnnkxw,"Listen to Songs of Aboriginal Australia and Torres Strait by Various Artists on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more.",Yinggarda,Australian
5,"Home Page | Gnulli Festival | Yinggarda, Carnarvon",https://www.gnullifestival.com.au/,"The Gnulli Festival is a vibrant celebration of community, culture and Country, held on Yinggarda Country (Carnarvon). It celebrates the Yinggarda and Baiyungu cultures that make up the Shire of Carnarvon, creating an opportunity to showcase our community, culture and Country ahead of the WA Tourism Conference. Through a dynamic program of live music, cultural experiences, food, art and ...",Yinggarda,Australian
6,"Yinggarda - Languages of the Gascoyne Region, Western Australia",https://yinggarda.org/welcome-to-the-yinggarda-language/languages-and-people/yinggarda/,"The territory which belonged to the Yinggarda people extended from the coast at the northern end of Shark Bay between the Gascoyne and Wooramel rivers, along the rivers inland to Red Hill and Gascoyne Junction. Their immediate neighbours were the Bayungu, Dharrgari and Warriyangga to the north, Malgana to the south, and Wajarri to the…",Yinggarda,Australian
7,"Languages of the Gascoyne Region, Western Australia",https://yinggarda.org/,"The groups who traditionally occupied this region are Yinggarda, Bayungu, Thalanyji, Burduna, Binigura, Tharrgari, Thiin, Warriyangga, and Jiwarli. We are gradually adding information on all of them, starting with Yinggarda.",Yinggarda,Australian
8,Songs of Aboriginal Australia and Torres Strait,http://earthtube.com/music/disco/disc64.html,・『THE AUSTRALIAN ABORIGINAL HERITAGE』 (2LP 1973 : Australian Society for Education Trough the Arts) ・『AUTHENTIC ABORIGINAL MUSIC -Music from the Wandjina People』 (CD 1995 : ARC),Yinggarda,Australian
9,Songs of Aboriginal Australia and Torres Strait,https://folkways.si.edu/songs-of-aboriginal-australia-and-torres-strait/world/music/album/smithsonian,"Despite making up only a small percentage of the country's total population, the aboriginal tribes of Australia are incredibly diverse and speak over 200 distinct languages. This recording features songs by aboriginal tribes from Western Australia, North Queensland, and the Torres Strait. Didjeridu player Albert (no last name given in liner notes), who uses a five foot didjeridu made from a ...",Yinggarda,Australian
